WEBVTT

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:02.590
Year 2195

00:00:02.590 --> 00:00:05.690
It came from beyond Jupiter.

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:05.740
Year 2195

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.030
The First Mars Battle

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:11.350
The enemy is heading directly towards Mars.

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:14.750
Projections show the enemy landing near the South Pole.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.310
It is clear that the enemy intends to invade.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:20.730
Do not let them reach Mars!

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:32.790
All vessels, fire at will as soon as they are within range!

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:34.410
The enemy continues to advance.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:37.190
Entering effective range of fire in twenty seconds!

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:49.880
Fire!

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.140
All our beam projectiles were repelled!

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:04.530
Gravitational waves?

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:10.020
Fire all lasers now!

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:14.710
No effect!

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:16.830
The Chulip has entered Mars orbit.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:19.820
In sixty seconds, it will reach the South Pole.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.130
All hands abandon ship!

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:23.460
We'll ram this ship into the Chulip!

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:57.350
To Go "Like a Man"!

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.010
Headquarters!

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:05.590
They might not be around anymore.

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:06.200
What?

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.250
I'm talking about the people on the surface.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:08.120
Damn, at this rate, everything above ground will be wiped out.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:09.310
This way, Doctor!

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:10.590
Damn, at this rate, everything above ground will be wiped out.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:11.940
Here.

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:14.210
Oh wow, thank you!

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:15.300
You're too kind!

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.310
It's nothing. I was coming back from the market.

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:19.400
Thank you Onii-chan!

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:20.090
Sure.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:21.260
Let's go on a date!

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:24.580
My name is Ai!

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.110
Watch out!

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:40.630
Right now, we are opening the doors manually.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:42.090
Please do not panic!

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:44.000
Make sure the civilians get out of here safely!

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:49.360
I'll distract them...

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:50.300
Run while you can!

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:52.720
Onii-chan!

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.330
I'm not finished yet!

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:13.010
You're so cool!

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:14.070
Good! The door's opened!

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:52.260
One year has passed since the defeat at the First Battle of Mars.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:55.990
Mars is completely fallen into enemy's hand.

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:59.130
It's only a matter of time before Earth falls as well.

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:01.170
I have a question.

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:02.870
Yes, what is it, Goat-kun?

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.790
What is it you would have me do?

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:07.920
Schiaparelli Project.

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:10.040
I believe you have heard about it.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:10.440
Yes.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.280
Even among us,

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:15.710
many have recommended you, who have much experience.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:17.640
Me?

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.180
Is this part of a military procurement?

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:24.430
Well, leaving that aside,
many girls will be part of this project.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.010
Hmm?

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:26.500
And a bonus.

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:28.070
Let me see...

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:30.460
How's this?

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:33.820
May I ask something?

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:34.480
Yes?

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:37.400
Is that after taxes?

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.400
Well, let's leave that aside,

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.750
and worry about the human resources required.

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:43.570
Human resources?

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:45.370
Yes, human resources.

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:47.490
The very best,

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:49.910
even if it means some with slight personality problems.

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:57.010
Honey, you've been at this for three days...

00:04:57.010 --> 00:04:57.830
Keep quiet!

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.300
After this, Lily-chan will be invincible!

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.640
Hello, please excuse us.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.510
It's not what you think! This...

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:07.400
Hello, my name is Lily.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.290
Hire me as a mechanic?

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:14.250
You may be making illegal alterations, but you're still quite talented.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:15.670
Please, won't you consider...

00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:19.300
All right, let's go. Let's go now!

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:21.570
But what about negotiating a contract?

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:22.740
Don't worry about it!

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:25.370
As long as I can get away from those two,
I don't care if the job is in Hell.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:26.800
Are you sure about this?

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:27.640
Letter of Resignation

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.830
Do you dislike being the secretary of the company president that much?

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:30.000
Letter of Resignation

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.300
Well, you know...

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:34.460
I guess it has more to do with job satisfaction.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:36.420
It's time for us to fight!

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:37.960
All right, let's go!

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:39.080
Yeah!

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:40.000
Good, OK!

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:41.860
Thank you!

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:43.230
Thank you!  Thanks!

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:43.980
Megumi-chan

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:44.260
Yes?

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:45.860
Visitor!

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.220
Someone from Nergal.

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:05.410
Yurika!

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:07.290
Yurika, see?

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:08.590
Your father's getting upset.

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:12.690
But this uniform is so not cool. I don't look right in it!

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:15.710
What's the use of worrying about that?

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:16.630
Say, Jun-kun...

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:21.000
Note : UEAF = United Earth Allied Forces
Are you sure it was a good idea to leave the UEAF and come with me?

00:06:21.670 --> 00:06:24.650
leaving you alone...makes me worried.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:27.440
As ever, Jun-kun, you're my best friend!

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:28.440
Sure, sure...

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:29.440
Yurika!

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:31.100
Damn it, Yurika!

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:32.970
I've had enough of this schoolgirl behavior.

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:33.890
But!

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:35.200
What do you mean "but"?!

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:35.990
She's getting dressed right now!

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:37.490
This is an important day for you...

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:43.370
Yurika, how you've grown.

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:49.500
To think that my own daughter would be so well endowed physically.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:52.850
Yurika, make your father proud with your deeds.

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:57.650
Jovian Lizards threaten the Earth!

00:06:57.650 --> 00:06:59.840
Punch them out with our united fists!

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:02.670
Protect the Earth! United we stand!

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:04.210
From the government...

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:06.370
There they go again.

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:07.930
Hey, what's holding up the stir-fried vegetables?

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:09.730
Hey!

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:11.220
What?  This again?

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:16.010
Oh boy, another one lost.

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:17.790
They're just not as maneuverable.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:19.180
They should just give up.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:21.380
Hey, it's more fun inside.

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:25.750
What's up with that guy?

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:27.380
Says he's scared.

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:28.050
Of what?

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:28.910
Them.

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:43.800
Oops, turn off the flames.

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:46.440
To start with,

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:48.440
here are your wages.

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:50.910
I'm fired?

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:52.490
Because of this.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:56.560
If rumors start that I'm sheltering run-away pilots.

00:07:56.560 --> 00:07:57.630
You mean this?

00:07:57.630 --> 00:07:58.920
It's not what you think...

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:01.020
People don't see it that way.

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:04.400
Besides, the way you get scared is just too much.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:06.770
But being a cook is all I have.

00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:09.910
You know, you'll never make anything of yourself.

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:11.560
If you keep running away.

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:14.250
Damn it!

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:16.160
What's wrong with running away?

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:18.080
Who cares?!

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:20.000
I'm scared of what I'm scared of!

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:22.770
Me too, I want to do something about it as well.

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:24.470
But my body...

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:26.640
My body! My body! My body!

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:28.920
Watch it!

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:37.440
I can't stand it anymore!

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:38.690
Why always me?

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:40.770
I'm terribly sorry. I'm terribly sorry!

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:42.490
I'm really sorry about this.

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:43.730
I'm so really sorry.

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:45.900
Did you hurt anywhere?

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:56.390
Hey, Yurika, let's leave something behind.

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:57.010
No!

00:08:57.350 --> 00:09:00.300
Those are all important things that I spent three days picking out!

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:01.590
We're taking it all along with us.

00:09:01.590 --> 00:09:02.490
Yeah, yeah.

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:05.090
Sorry for the trouble, you even help me repack.

00:09:05.090 --> 00:09:05.920
Sure, sure.

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:09.210
No problem, you're just not good with packing stuff.

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:09.990
Really?

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:13.040
You need to consolidate what you can,

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:15.800
and use clothes as packing material to protect other things.

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:16.520
Eh?

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:21.020
Ah? . . . Eh? . . . AA!

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:25.420
Ahhhh! ...  I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:26.320
Excuse me,

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:29.110
I know this might sound a little inconsiderate, but...

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:29.610
Yes?

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:32.270
Have we met before?

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:35.360
I can't help but feel that we have.

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:38.360
Really? I can't say I feel that way.

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:40.190
I see.

00:09:40.190 --> 00:09:41.210
Yurika!

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:42.810
Yes...!

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:46.230
Thank you for your cooperation.

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:46.720
Bye!

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:50.720
That case is not going into the backseat, or the trunk.

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:52.140
Yes..!

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:54.810
There she goes dropping something again.

00:09:57.470 --> 00:09:59.140
This... This is me!

00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:01.390
Why me?

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:02.700
That woman...

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:03.260
Why?

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:07.650
Have we met before?

00:10:08.150 --> 00:10:09.570
Oh yes, we have!

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:10.980
We have! We have!

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:12.280
Yurika!

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:13.410
Misumaru Yurika!

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:17.080
I know exactly who you are!

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:19.620
I need to know! I need to know!

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:21.920
Just you wait!

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:23.230
Yurika!

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:32.990
Nergal Heavy Industries - Basement Dock's Entrance

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:35.420
Wait? What's the meaning of this?!

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:36.450
You don't need any of us except Admiral Fukube?!...

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:37.610
BAKA-bakka!

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:37.960
You don't need any of us except Admiral Fukube?!...

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:39.550
It's them, right?

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:42.040
The ones who dropped a battleship on top of the Mars colony?

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:44.980
I can see where there would be complaints about that.

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:47.340
The crew are all talented experts in their own fields.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:50.450
And the captain graduated from the United Earth University,

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:54.410
and was undefeated in all integrated strategic simulation battles.

00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:57.000
So, where is this genius?

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:57.910
Well...

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:00.380
Wow! This must be it!

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:02.230
Everyone.

00:11:02.230 --> 00:11:04.660
I am the captain!

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:05.840
V!

00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:07.690
V?!

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:08.540
Another Idiot?

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:11.190
With this, I'm sure to catch everyone's heart!

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:16.400
He was at the front gate causing a riot,
so we took him into custody.

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:18.630
Let me go! Yurika!

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:20.980
Well, I see that you are a pilot.

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:22.600
No! I'm a cook.

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:26.420
He's been ranting like that the whole time.

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:31.450
Let's find out what your name really is.

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:32.490
DNA database?

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:33.530
Here we go!

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:38.520
How did you escape the destruction of the Utopia Colony, and get here?

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:43.180
I can't remember much of what happened then.

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:45.790
Next thing I knew, I was on Earth.

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:48.190
Are you an acquaintance of Yurika-san?

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:49.940
Back on Mars Colony.

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:52.290
She and her family...

00:11:52.630 --> 00:11:55.430
She should knows why my parents died.

00:11:57.790 --> 00:11:59.190
I see.

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:01.310
That must have been rough on you.

00:12:03.340 --> 00:12:06.200
You say you're a cook?

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:07.260
All right.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:11.440
From now on, you will be a cook on the Nadesico.

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:13.810
Make sure to work hard!

00:12:13.810 --> 00:12:14.880
Nadesico?

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:17.530
That's right. The Nadesico!

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:21.130
The ship won't take off for some time,

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:23.470
so you might want to walk around, and get to know the ship.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:24.290
Okay.

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:28.450
Let's go!

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:30.570
Gekiganger!

00:12:30.570 --> 00:12:34.710
Not Gekiganger. The name is Aestivalis.

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:36.510
I'll finish you off with

00:12:36.740 --> 00:12:38.330
Gekigan Blade!

00:12:38.330 --> 00:12:40.430
Hey, hey! Hey you!

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:41.920
What is this about?!

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:44.090
Pilots aren't supposed to report for another three days!

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:50.440
When I heard we get to pilot real robots, I couldn't hold myself back.

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:53.110
Tada, tada! Kabooom!

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:54.510
What, what?!

00:12:54.510 --> 00:12:55.530
What are you doing?!

00:12:55.890 --> 00:12:57.510
I'll let only you know.

00:12:57.820 --> 00:13:01.370
Gai-sama's hyper, ultra-cool, great killer move!

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:03.000
I call it,

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:03.530
What?

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:08.790
Gai Super Napalm!

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:10.180
What?!

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:14.300
Gekiganger, huh?

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.430
This is too cool! It's a real robot!

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:20.940
It has arms and legs, and moves exactly as you wish it to.

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:22.490
It's just too cool!

00:13:22.490 --> 00:13:25.040
Thanks to the latest in lmage Feedback technology.

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:28.000
With that even a child could move one around.

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:29.630
I'm Gai.

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:30.830
Daigoji Gai!

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:32.240
Just call me Gai!

00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:35.740
It says Yamada Jirou in your profile.

00:13:35.740 --> 00:13:37.130
That's temporary name.

00:13:37.130 --> 00:13:40.540
My soul's name is Daigoji Gai. That's my real name!

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:43.730
Evil Jovians, come if you dare!

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:44.780
Eh?!

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:45.750
What is it?

00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:46.740
Well...

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:49.940
My leg really hurts.

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:53.420
Stupid Otaku, your leg is broken!

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:54.850
What?!

00:13:56.710 --> 00:13:58.870
Hey, that boy there!

00:13:58.870 --> 00:13:59.220
Eh?

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:04.000
I left my important treasure in the cockpit.

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:05.640
Would you go get it for me?

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:10.240
His treasure is a Gekiganger robot toy?

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:11.700
Just how old is he?

00:14:13.340 --> 00:14:13.860
What's going on?

00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:16.800
Our ground forces have engaged enemy tactical weapons.

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:17.810
All bridge crew, report to the combat command center immediately.

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:18.440
It's them!

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:18.750
All bridge crew, report to the combat command center immediately.

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:20.130
They have come!

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:20.140
All bridge crew, report to the combat command center immediately.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:23.670
I repeat, all bridge crew, report to the combat command center.

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:29.490
Why there?

00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:31.450
I can't figure out what the Jovians are thinking.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.890
I wonder if he's trembling again?

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:41.170
The enemy is concentrating their attack directly over our position.

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:43.810
Is the Nadesico their target?

00:14:43.810 --> 00:14:45.580
If that's the case, we'll counterattack!

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:46.180
How?

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:50.670
We'll use the Nadesico's anti-aircraft fire to burn them to a crisp.

00:14:50.670 --> 00:14:53.360
And destroy our own men fighting above too?

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:55.090
They're going to be annihilated one way or another.

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:58.120
Wouldn't you call that being cold-blooded?

00:14:58.900 --> 00:15:01.110
Captain, do you have any suggestions?

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:04.170
We will launch through the underwater dock into the ocean.

00:15:04.490 --> 00:15:06.540
Once there, we'll emerge behind the enemy,

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:07.950
and neutralize them!

00:15:08.360 --> 00:15:10.520
Here's where I come in!

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:13.600
I'll deploy the robot against the enemy, and lure them inland.

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:15.930
In the meantime, the Nadesico can launch.

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:18.350
Oh, what a burning situation.

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:20.270
Otaku, you just broke you leg!

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:21.420
Oh no!

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:23.290
A decoy has already taken off.

00:15:23.290 --> 00:15:23.840
Eh?

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:26.290
There's a robot in the elevator...

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:30.680
I'm sick of being cooped up.

00:15:31.350 --> 00:15:33.000
I'm going to be a cook!

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:34.680
Screw getting killed in battle.

00:15:35.020 --> 00:15:36.110
Who are you?

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:37.400
Are you a pilot?

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:38.440
Er. No...

00:15:38.440 --> 00:15:41.530
Hey, he's taking my Gekiganger!

00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:42.870
State your name and position.

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:44.630
Tenkawa Akito, cook.

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:45.320
What?!

00:15:45.640 --> 00:15:47.250
Yurika, that person...

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.130
Um, Tenkawa...

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:51.300
What the hell is he doing in the cockpit?

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:53.270
He's from Mars.

00:15:53.270 --> 00:15:54.870
I hired him as a cook.

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:56.610
So, what's a cook doing inside an Aestivalis?

00:15:56.610 --> 00:15:57.330
Akito?

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:00.530
Akito! It's Akito!

00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:04.350
It's been so long. It's really you, Akito!

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:06.700
Why did you pretend to not know me?

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:09.220
I get it! You're still the same shy boy I used to know.

00:16:09.220 --> 00:16:10.960
Hey, wait just one second!

00:16:10.960 --> 00:16:12.960
What are you doing there anyway?

00:16:12.960 --> 00:16:15.860
She's the captain of the Nadesico.

00:16:16.510 --> 00:16:19.440
That's right! Ms. Yurika Misumaru is the captain of the Nadesico!

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:20.380
Ahem!

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:22.870
Hey, wait, Yurika, who is guy anyway?

00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:25.440
Un, he's my prince.

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:28.530
He always comes to my aid whenever I'm in trouble.

00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:29.620
Hey, wait just second, damn it!

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:32.650
But, I can't let you act as a decoy. It's too dangerous.

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:33.910
Hey, what decoy?

00:16:34.310 --> 00:16:36.610
But I know how you are once you've made up your mind.

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:39.100
I suppose the words of a passionate woman won't stop you.

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:39.460
Hey, wait!

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:40.820
I understand.

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:45.070
I'll trust you with the fate of the Nadesico and all her crew.

00:16:45.070 --> 00:16:47.340
Please survive and come back.

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:50.320
Damn it, come back here!

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:52.390
Elevator slowing. You are about to reach the ground level.

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:53.470
Wait...

00:16:53.470 --> 00:16:54.720
Good luck!

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:56.370
Give me back my Gekiganger!

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:57.860
Shut UP!

00:16:58.900 --> 00:17:00.400
You have ten minutes.

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:01.910
Just keep the enemy occupied.

00:17:02.270 --> 00:17:03.540
Best wishes to you.

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:17.080
I'll trust you with the fate of the Nadesico and all her crew.

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:23.750
This is dirty!

00:17:24.340 --> 00:17:25.670
Making me a decoy!

00:17:28.450 --> 00:17:31.510
Damn it! Go back, and fight them like a man!

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:34.430
Impossible! How is a cook supposed to know how to fight?

00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:36.760
Now, is the time to unleash our anti-aircraft weapons!

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:38.360
He's doing quite well.

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:39.940
Indeed, an excellent decoy.

00:17:39.940 --> 00:17:41.770
Akito, I won't let you die!

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:44.880
Flooding 80% complete. Opening underwater gate.

00:17:48.010 --> 00:17:49.980
Engines ready.

00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:51.410
Nadesico, launch!

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:53.160
Nadesico launching.

00:17:57.310 --> 00:17:58.080
Another seven minutes?!

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:00.540
How the hell am I supposed to keep running for another seven minutes?!

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:04.900
Damn! Damn!

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:07.840
I've had enough of this!

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:19.670
Cool! Just like a Gekigan Punch.

00:18:20.350 --> 00:18:22.380
The hell with it then!

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:33.280
Gee, I'm not too bad at this after all.

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:35.830
But, too late now.

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:47.420
What now?!

00:19:17.560 --> 00:19:18.590
Wow...

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:20.570
Sorry to keep you waiting, Akito.

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:24.110
What do you mean? It hasn't been ten minutes yet.

00:19:24.110 --> 00:19:25.540
I rushed for your sake.

00:19:25.800 --> 00:19:28.460
Remaining enemy forces are almost all within our effective field of fire.

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:31.920
Target all the enemy we can reach!

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:32.880
Fire!

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:38.070
Awesome!

00:19:39.310 --> 00:19:40.960
Give me a situation report.

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:42.640
Note : Batta = Grasshopper.
There are no Battas or Zeroes remaining.

00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:46.340
Ground forces were hit hard, but only five deaths have been reported.

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:48.560
No way! It can't be! It has to be luck!

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:50.400
Recognize her achievements.

00:19:50.400 --> 00:19:51.590
You did a good job, Captain.

00:19:51.590 --> 00:19:52.790
True brilliance!

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:55.280
Akito! You were amazing! Really amazing!

00:19:55.990 --> 00:19:57.200
Don't get it wrong.

00:19:57.200 --> 00:19:59.400
I didn't come here to save you or anything.

00:19:59.400 --> 00:20:00.540
I came here to see you, and...

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:01.960
You came to see me?!

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:04.230
No! I just saw this, and...

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:08.560
That photograph! I see!
You came all this way to bring that back to me?

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:10.380
Oh, I'm so glad.

00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:14.380
Stop playing around! Depending on what I find out, I'm going to m...

00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:15.840
Meet me? Marry me?

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:17.220
Oh, you're rushing things too much!

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:17.930
No!

00:20:18.290 --> 00:20:19.990
Yes, of course. That wouldn't be the case!

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:22.090
Something like that comes after spending time with each other.

00:20:22.090 --> 00:20:24.060
I'm a little worried about the future here.

00:20:24.060 --> 00:20:26.100
But it looks like it'll be interesting here.

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:28.270
Who cares about that. I want my Gekiganger back!

00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:29.770
Listen to me for once!

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:32.280
I know. I know exactly how Akito feels.

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:34.070
You don't know anything about me!

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:35.180
You're making me...

00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:35.480
Crazy in love for me, right?

00:20:35.480 --> 00:20:36.240
BAKA-bakka!

00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:37.800
I want to make it clear that I...

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:38.580
Love me!

00:20:38.580 --> 00:20:39.450
No!

00:20:39.450 --> 00:20:40.880
Love me very, very much!

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:42.790
Listen to someone else for once!

00:21:47.520 --> 00:21:48.790
Sound the cannon!

00:21:48.790 --> 00:21:50.230
Nadesico, launch!

00:21:50.720 --> 00:21:53.650
Evil extends its hands to obstruct the path of our beloved Nadesico!

00:21:53.650 --> 00:21:56.280
Why must man fight against man?

00:21:56.280 --> 00:22:01.170
The captain holds back her tears in the face of cruel fate and separation!

00:22:01.170 --> 00:22:02.620
A barrage of breathtakingly suspenseful moments!

00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:07.250
Nadesico's new journey begins in the air where the Aestivalis flies proud!

00:22:07.250 --> 00:22:11.950
Next Nadesico: "Leave the Blue Earth to Me"!

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:13.690
Let's watch with everyone!
